# camie-immich-tagger cron examples.
#
# Install for the runtime account with: crontab -e
# These are user-crontab entries (no username column), in the server's timezone.
# Adjust the checkout path everywhere if you did not use the README default.
#
# Requirements: /usr/bin/flock (util-linux), mounted image storage, and read/write
# permissions for configuration, sidecars, logs and state. The runtime account
# must be able to create/open LOCK; choose a protected writable path if non-root.
# Use this same lock for manual runs and other jobs touching the same state.
# A busy lock skips a run; it does not wait. Immich jobs continue asynchronously.
# The tool writes its own rotating log. Monitor cron output/exit status too.
# See operations.md for scheduling, account permissions and import caveats.

CAMIE=/opt/camie-immich-tagger-linux/venv/bin/camie-tagger
LOCK=/run/lock/camie-tagger.lock

# Every night at 03:00: tag new images, then let Immich import the sidecars.
0 3 * * * /usr/bin/flock -n "$LOCK" "$CAMIE" run --mode recent --immich-scan

# Alternative: REPLACE the entry above with a sequential Tier 0 workflow.
# This uploads eligible images to SauceNAO and uses the configured per-run quota.
# Local tagging --limit does not cap subsequent Tier 0 searches.
# 0 3 * * * /usr/bin/flock -n "$LOCK" "$CAMIE" run --mode recent --tier0 --immich-scan

# Destructive cleanup is intentionally not scheduled. Review previews manually
# and verify storage mounts before considering cleanup-orphans --confirm.
# cleanup-tags can delete manual Immich tags globally, not just this library.
